# [Count Islands With Total Value Divisible by K](https://leetcode.com/problems/count-islands-with-total-value-divisible-by-k/)

## Approach: DFS (Depth-First Search)

We traverse the grid and use DFS to find each connected island of non-zero cells. For every island, we calculate the sum of its cell values and check whether the sum is divisible by `k`.

### Code (C++)

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    void solve(vector<vector<int>>& grid, vector<vector<int>>& vis,
               int row, int col, long long& sum,
               vector<pair<int,int>>& dir) {
        if (row < 0 || col < 0 || row >= grid.size() ||
            col >= grid[0].size() || vis[row][col]) return;

        vis[row][col] = 1;
        sum += grid[row][col];

        for (const auto& it : dir) {
            int r = row + it.first;
            int c = col + it.second;

            if (r < 0 || c < 0 || r >= grid.size() ||
                c >= grid[0].size() || vis[r][c] ||
                grid[r][c] == 0) continue;

            solve(grid, vis, r, c, sum, dir);
        }
    }

    int countIslands(vector<vector<int>>& grid, int k) {
        int row = grid.size(), col = grid[0].size();

        vector<vector<int>> vis(row, vector<int>(col, 0));
        vector<pair<int,int>> dir = {
            {-1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, -1}
        };

        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < row; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < col; j++) {
                if (!vis[i][j] && grid[i][j] != 0) {
                    long long sum = 0;
                    solve(grid, vis, i, j, sum, dir);

                    if (sum % k == 0) count++;
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
};
```

### Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(m \times n)\), where \(m\) is the number of rows and \(n\) is the number of columns. Every cell is visited at most once.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(m \times n)\) for the visited matrix, with additional recursion stack space of up to \(O(m \times n)\) in the worst case.

### Key Points

- An island consists of connected non-zero cells.
- Only four-directional adjacency is considered.
- Each island's total value is calculated independently.
- An island is counted if `sum % k == 0`.
